.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt XLOCK-RUN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xlock-run
.Nd run xlock under a chosen WM_CLASS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Ar class Ar xlock
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Ar xlock
with
.Ar args
and sets the locker window's
.Ev WM_CLASS
instance to
.Ar class
and its class to
.Cm xlock .
.Pp
.Ar class
.Cm xlock-screen
is kept opaque.
A black underlay covers the screen and is restacked under the
saver for the whole lock, so a random mode that opens and closes
windows cannot show the desktop.
The saver's opacity property is set fully opaque.
.Pp
Any other
.Ar class ,
including
.Cm xlock-desktop ,
gets no underlay, and the opacity property is removed so a
compositor can show the session through the saver.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits non-zero when the display cannot be opened or the arguments
are missing.
Otherwise it exits with the status of
.Ar xlock .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xlock 1 ,
.Xr xlock-invoke 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
